<title>USA: Life Financial IPO size increased.</title>
<headline>Life Financial IPO size increased.</headline>
<dateline>RIVERSIDE, Calif. 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Life Financial Corp Monday said Keefe, Bruyette &amp; Woods Inc, underwriter of the company's initial public offering, has exercised its over-allotment option to acquire an additional 435,000 shares.</p>
<p>The company sold the shares at $11.00 per share, raising additional gross proceeds of about $4.8 million.</p>
<p>Life Financial is the holding company for Life Savings Bank. Its shares climbed 2-1/8 to 16-5/8 near the end of the day on Monday.</p>
</text>
